WEBVTT

00:00.125 --> 00:04.796
I need to know the truth
about Hijikata Toshizo.

00:04.880 --> 00:09.301
He had the same look
in his eyes as you.

00:09.384 --> 00:13.347
What's the fun
in doing the sensible thing?

00:13.430 --> 00:17.476
[Hijikata]
Doing what no one else can
is what makes you a badass.

00:17.559 --> 00:20.604
[Kondo] This guy...
he might be a good fit for us.

00:20.687 --> 00:22.940
[narrator] The time: the final
years of the Edo period.

00:23.023 --> 00:24.608
Gathered at the Shieikan dojo

00:24.691 --> 00:27.027
home of the Tennen
Rishin-ryu style...

00:27.110 --> 00:30.531
We'll have another match,
Toshizo.

00:30.614 --> 00:33.534
[narrator]
...were ten fearsome warriors,
including Hijikata Toshizo.

00:33.617 --> 00:35.118
[Serizawa]
After all, the one thing that

00:35.160 --> 00:36.119
really gets
a man's blood pumping

00:36.161 --> 00:37.454
is good old-fashioned violence.

00:37.496 --> 00:39.039
Ain't that right?

00:39.122 --> 00:42.584
I swear...
I'll never lose to anyone again.

00:42.668 --> 00:45.712
[narrator]
This was a turbulent era.

00:45.796 --> 00:51.593
This is the story of men who
lived and died by the sword.

00:53.178 --> 00:55.180
Tennen Rishin-ryu:
Sword of No Light!

00:57.182 --> 01:03.730
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

01:13.198 --> 01:14.866
FEBRUARY, 1863

01:14.950 --> 01:17.661
[narrator] February, 1863.

01:17.744 --> 01:20.163
The men of the Shieikan dojo
came to Kyo

01:20.247 --> 01:22.164
seeking
to become the strongest.

01:23.667 --> 01:27.295
But they were unable to find
a way to make a living

01:27.337 --> 01:31.466
let alone make a name for
themselves with their swords.

01:33.343 --> 01:35.929
[grunts]
[blood gushing]

01:36.013 --> 01:37.389
Meanwhile...

01:42.185 --> 01:44.646
You bastard!
You're a manslayer!

01:45.354 --> 01:46.982
[yells]

01:47.065 --> 01:49.568
[blood spilling, gurgles]

01:51.652 --> 01:54.156
DIVINE RETRIBUTION

01:54.239 --> 01:55.949
[narrator] Aizu clan samurai,
shogunate allies

01:56.033 --> 01:59.411
were being attacked
one after another,

01:59.494 --> 02:02.122
terrorizing the city of Kyo.

02:02.205 --> 02:03.540
[shouts]
[groans]

02:10.172 --> 02:12.424
[dog barking]

02:20.265 --> 02:23.310
ONE MONTH LATER

02:24.311 --> 02:26.228
[people chattering indistinctly]

02:26.313 --> 02:28.440
[music playing indistinctly]

02:49.168 --> 02:50.754
This is good.

02:50.796 --> 02:51.922
[crunching]

02:51.963 --> 02:53.298
Mm.

02:53.382 --> 02:56.218
[Hijikata]
This isn't enough.

02:56.301 --> 02:58.220
[Nagakura]
By the way, Eisaburo.

02:58.303 --> 03:01.098
What were you up to last night?

03:01.181 --> 03:03.058
Huh? Hmm?

03:03.141 --> 03:04.476
Well...

03:04.559 --> 03:07.104
You smelled of face powder
when you came back.

03:07.145 --> 03:08.105
[men giggling]
[gasps]

03:08.188 --> 03:10.774
Don't tell me you were this?

03:10.816 --> 03:13.193
You're more of a player
than you look, you sly dog!

03:13.276 --> 03:15.862
No, that's not it!
Where would I get that money?

03:15.946 --> 03:17.656
Hmm. Suspicious.

03:17.739 --> 03:18.740
It's not like that.

03:18.824 --> 03:20.742
[taunting playfully]

03:20.826 --> 03:23.620
[Yamanami]
If we had that kind of money...

03:23.662 --> 03:25.622
[Todo] You wanted to go
with him too, Yamanami?

03:25.664 --> 03:26.873
Of course not!

03:28.125 --> 03:29.418
[Hijikata]
I'm hungry.

03:29.501 --> 03:31.795
If we don't find a way
to make a living today,

03:31.878 --> 03:33.714
our savings will run out.

03:35.257 --> 03:36.841
[sighing]
Fine.

03:39.845 --> 03:42.347
[Sasaki]
Hello? Anyone home?

03:42.430 --> 03:43.807
[Hijikata]
Hey!

03:43.849 --> 03:47.310
Still stinks like a bunch
of sweaty guys in here.

03:47.352 --> 03:49.438
Sasaki Tadasaburo?
What're you doing here?

03:49.521 --> 03:52.232
Hey, hey.
Please calm down.

03:52.315 --> 03:54.442
Mr. Sasaki was also
a shogunate official

03:54.526 --> 03:55.944
involved with the Roshigumi.

03:56.027 --> 04:00.323
Ah... He got screwed over
by Kiyokawa, same as us.

04:00.365 --> 04:02.701
[laughs]
What gives?

04:02.784 --> 04:05.454
An official
who's officially useless?

04:05.495 --> 04:11.543
Seriously?
Don't talk to me, you monkey.

04:13.044 --> 04:15.464
The only ones here
worth talking to

04:18.091 --> 04:20.969
are you and you.

04:26.516 --> 04:29.227
I presume
you've heard the rumors

04:29.311 --> 04:31.104
about manslayers
targeting shogunate retainers.

04:31.188 --> 04:32.898
[Kondo] Yes.
We've heard they're assassins

04:32.981 --> 04:34.775
sent by the Imperialists.

04:34.858 --> 04:38.320
Naturally, we can't just let
scoundrels like that run wild.

04:38.361 --> 04:42.157
And so, an order has come down
from the powers that be.

04:42.240 --> 04:45.034
To gather
all swordsmen of skill.

04:45.118 --> 04:46.787
[Kondo]
Does that mean...

04:46.870 --> 04:50.040
we have a chance
to serve the shogunate?

04:50.081 --> 04:51.374
[Sasaki]
Precisely.

04:52.459 --> 04:54.211
Giving this job
to savages like you...

04:54.252 --> 04:55.670
Personally, I was against it.

04:55.754 --> 04:58.215
Is that true? Is that true?
[clamoring happily]

04:58.256 --> 05:00.383
You're not so bad after all.

05:00.467 --> 05:03.845
This is why I hate you savages!

05:03.929 --> 05:05.347
What?

05:05.430 --> 05:06.973
[Yamanami] Sasaki.
Yes?

05:07.057 --> 05:09.226
Is what you just said true?

05:09.309 --> 05:11.561
Will the shogunate
really take us in?

05:11.603 --> 05:13.522
Yes, but there's a catch.

05:13.605 --> 05:16.691
The Aizu will test you.
[Nagakura] The Aizu?

05:16.775 --> 05:17.692
That's right.

05:17.776 --> 05:20.487
To see if you're actually
of any use.

05:20.570 --> 05:23.114
And what if we fail
to get Aizu's approval?

05:23.198 --> 05:25.826
Then you'd better be
prepared to starve.

05:25.909 --> 05:27.118
Bring it on!

05:27.202 --> 05:29.037
They're more than a worthy test!

05:29.120 --> 05:30.580
We'll show them what we've got!

05:30.622 --> 05:32.957
[shouting determinedly]

05:33.041 --> 05:34.417
[♪♪♪]

05:34.501 --> 05:40.340
KYOTO MILITARY COMMISSIONER
AIZU DOMAIN HEADQUARTERS

05:40.423 --> 05:43.677
[Hijikata] What the hell
are they doing here?

05:43.760 --> 05:47.639
[Sasaki] Serizawa Kamo,
Niimi Nishiki, Hirayama Goro.

05:47.722 --> 05:50.100
Word that they defied
Kiyokawa Hachiro

05:50.183 --> 05:52.352
has reached the ears
of the Shogunate.

05:52.435 --> 05:54.479
They're considered
men of real grit.

05:55.355 --> 05:57.482
Especially Serizawa Kamo.

05:57.566 --> 05:59.609
The man's a monster in a fight.

05:59.651 --> 06:03.113
And where the hell's Kamo?

06:03.154 --> 06:07.909
Master Serizawa went out last
night and has yet to return.

06:09.327 --> 06:10.996
Hmph. The nerve of him.

06:12.831 --> 06:15.000
[wooden swords clashing]
[fierce yelling]

06:16.501 --> 06:18.670
[exclaims]
[laughing]

06:23.008 --> 06:25.552
[Nagakura] Toshi! Toshi! Toshi!
Don't go in there.

06:25.635 --> 06:27.512
[Abiru]
They are really fired up.

06:27.596 --> 06:31.433
[Yamanami] The Aizu are called
Japan's strongest.

06:31.516 --> 06:33.058
[Hijikata]
The strongest in Japan?

06:33.143 --> 06:35.020
That's right.

06:35.103 --> 06:37.647
The Aizu Domain,
ruled by the Matsudaira of Aizu

06:37.731 --> 06:39.357
is a prestigious clan
renowned

06:39.441 --> 06:41.318
for its unwavering loyalty
to the Tokugawa family.

06:41.359 --> 06:43.069
Their lord, Matsudaira Katamori

06:43.153 --> 06:45.989
was named as the Military
Commissioner of Kyoto

06:46.072 --> 06:49.993
and 1000 of his hand-picked men
are keeping the peace in Kyo.

06:52.287 --> 06:53.538
[Sagawa]
Line up!

07:03.298 --> 07:05.175
Who's that?

07:05.258 --> 07:06.843
That's Sagawa Kanbei.

07:06.885 --> 07:07.844
Sagawa...

07:09.512 --> 07:11.014
What is a samurai?

07:11.097 --> 07:12.515
[Sasaki]
That's him.

07:12.557 --> 07:14.351
They call him
"Kanbei the Demon."

07:14.392 --> 07:15.769
The greatest in all of Aizu...

07:15.852 --> 07:18.605
No, it wouldn't be
an exaggeration to call him

07:18.688 --> 07:20.523
the greatest samurai in Japan.
[Aizu warrior] A samurai is...

07:20.565 --> 07:23.526
The greatest in Japan, huh?

07:23.610 --> 07:26.321
He is the very embodiment
of a samurai.

07:26.404 --> 07:28.156
SAGAWA KANBEI

07:35.330 --> 07:37.499
It's been a while, Sasaki.

07:37.582 --> 07:40.043
You seem to be
in very high spirits.

07:40.085 --> 07:41.086
I'm glad.

07:42.420 --> 07:44.297
You're from
the former Roshigumi?

07:44.381 --> 07:45.507
Yes.

07:47.300 --> 07:48.718
I'm Kondo Isami,

07:48.802 --> 07:51.888
the 4th-generation master
of the Tennen Rishin-ryu school.

07:51.972 --> 07:53.765
Ah, yes.
I was told you were the ones

07:53.848 --> 07:55.767
with the backbone
to defy Kiyokawa.

07:57.268 --> 07:58.603
Hey, he says we've got backbone.

07:58.687 --> 08:00.689
When really we were just broke.

08:00.772 --> 08:02.524
Whatever.
It's a minor detail.

08:02.607 --> 08:04.067
[Aizu retainer]
How insolent!

08:04.150 --> 08:05.193
[blow thwacks]

08:08.697 --> 08:10.407
[Serizawa, groaning]
I'm here.

08:10.448 --> 08:13.576
SERIZAWA KAMO

08:13.660 --> 08:16.830
[Hijikata]
Serizawa...

08:19.541 --> 08:21.584
Ah, so you're the greatest
in all of Aizu,

08:21.626 --> 08:22.961
"Sagawa the Demon," huh?

08:23.712 --> 08:24.963
The one and only.

08:26.673 --> 08:29.384
I like it.
He reeks of pure mayhem.

08:29.467 --> 08:30.969
The finest vintage.

08:32.595 --> 08:37.017
All I smell on you
is face powder.

08:37.100 --> 08:39.727
[♪♪♪]

08:43.356 --> 08:44.774
So cold.

08:45.900 --> 08:47.068
Hey, move.

08:48.361 --> 08:50.113
Then let's not waste any time.

08:50.155 --> 08:51.823
Show me what you're made of.

08:53.366 --> 08:55.368
We humbly accept.

08:55.452 --> 08:57.495
I shall be your opponent.

08:57.579 --> 08:58.997
If you are victorious...

08:59.080 --> 09:02.667
I will recommend you to
our lord, Matsudaira Katamori.

09:05.795 --> 09:08.173
We're going to face
the Demon Chief himself...

09:08.256 --> 09:09.674
He's Japan's greatest samurai!

09:09.758 --> 09:11.509
[Sagawa] Bring the gear.
[Aizu retainer] Sir!

09:11.593 --> 09:12.886
Hold on a minute.

09:13.803 --> 09:15.764
What's the problem?

09:15.847 --> 09:17.682
We don't need that junk.

09:17.766 --> 09:19.893
Toshi, stand down!

09:21.061 --> 09:23.271
Anyone who'd get cold feet
just facing you

09:24.814 --> 09:26.941
isn't someone you'd want
in your ranks anyway, right?

09:27.025 --> 09:28.610
Hmm...

09:30.820 --> 09:32.572
Judging by your tone...

09:33.698 --> 09:35.617
I take it you'll be my opponent?

09:37.577 --> 09:38.787
That's right.

09:39.788 --> 09:41.539
I'm gonna beat you senseless.

09:41.623 --> 09:43.500
[Yamanami]
Hijikata, what are you doing?

09:43.540 --> 09:44.876
You'd better be ready!

09:45.710 --> 09:48.379
[♪♪♪]

09:48.463 --> 09:50.215
[stammers]

09:58.264 --> 10:02.060
You!
[yelling]

10:02.811 --> 10:04.687
Such incredible spirit.

10:04.771 --> 10:06.731
[groaning] Hey!
I like this man.

10:06.815 --> 10:09.025
It takes one to know one.

10:09.067 --> 10:10.068
Hey.

10:10.151 --> 10:14.155
Thank you.
Stop it! Stop it now! Creepy!

10:14.239 --> 10:15.615
Tell me your name!

10:17.075 --> 10:18.660
What is your name?

10:19.577 --> 10:20.870
Go.

10:21.830 --> 10:23.164
Hijikata Toshizo.

10:23.248 --> 10:24.666
Hijikata...

10:25.708 --> 10:27.127
That's a great name.

10:27.210 --> 10:29.003
[gunshot]

10:29.087 --> 10:30.004
My Lord!

10:39.806 --> 10:41.224
[Matsudaira]
Kanbei.

10:41.307 --> 10:42.809
Sir!

10:42.892 --> 10:45.186
[Matsudaira] What is the meaning
of this charade?

10:45.228 --> 10:48.064
That's Lord Matsudaira
of the Aizu Domain!

10:48.148 --> 10:49.858
Hurry up and bow down!

10:51.901 --> 10:53.278
You're not planning

10:55.405 --> 10:57.949
to fight them with a stick,
are you?

10:59.492 --> 11:00.451
[Sagawa gasps]

11:01.828 --> 11:03.121
LORD OF THE AIZU DOMAIN
MATSUDAIRA KATAMORI

11:03.204 --> 11:05.748
You think you can tell
if they're real samurai,

11:05.832 --> 11:07.083
risking their lives

11:08.877 --> 11:11.171
with something like that?

11:18.970 --> 11:20.388
[rings]

11:21.848 --> 11:23.141
[sheath clatters]

11:29.147 --> 11:31.107
Use this.

11:31.191 --> 11:32.483
A real sword...

11:34.152 --> 11:35.778
Cut the crap.

11:35.820 --> 11:39.699
If we use a real sword,
the loser is going to die!

11:39.782 --> 11:41.784
Get a hold of yourself.

11:41.868 --> 11:43.786
Then you can die for all I care.

11:43.870 --> 11:46.831
[♪♪♪]

11:54.839 --> 11:56.466
All right, listen up, bastards!

11:59.552 --> 12:01.012
Sooner or later

12:03.806 --> 12:05.391
the Shogunate is going to fall.

12:05.475 --> 12:08.686
[murmuring softly]

12:08.770 --> 12:10.813
Kyo is a battlefield now!

12:10.897 --> 12:14.275
It's kill or be killed.
That's all there is to it.

12:15.526 --> 12:18.029
In this Kyo, we Aizu were told

12:19.405 --> 12:23.284
to become the sacrificial pawns
of a dying shogunate!

12:23.368 --> 12:25.328
[Sagawa]
My Lord.

12:25.411 --> 12:27.247
And yet...

12:27.330 --> 12:30.500
Why did you accept the post
of Protector of Kyoto?

12:31.542 --> 12:33.044
It's obvious.

12:41.678 --> 12:42.971
Because I'm...

12:45.431 --> 12:47.433
Matsudaira Katamori.

12:55.233 --> 12:56.276
But listen.

12:58.027 --> 13:01.072
I don't intend to let
these men die for nothing.

13:05.076 --> 13:06.953
Losing without
even putting up a fight

13:07.036 --> 13:09.956
is not Katamori's way. No...

13:11.082 --> 13:14.294
it's not the Aizu way
of the samurai!

13:14.377 --> 13:16.379
If we're going to fight,

13:16.462 --> 13:18.965
we'll fight to the bitter end,

13:19.048 --> 13:21.134
even if the shogunate
itself surrenders.

13:22.093 --> 13:23.928
That is the Aizu way!

13:25.179 --> 13:26.222
My Lord!

13:26.264 --> 13:29.851
[all] My Lord!

13:29.934 --> 13:33.813
My Lord!
My Lord!

13:33.896 --> 13:39.652
[all] My Lord!

13:39.736 --> 13:41.112
Understand?

13:43.114 --> 13:46.284
Every last Aizu samurai here

13:47.452 --> 13:51.122
is a damn fool prepared
to die alongside me.

13:53.750 --> 13:56.669
That's what it means

13:56.753 --> 13:58.421
to fight with us.

14:04.135 --> 14:07.513
[chuckles]
I like it.

14:07.597 --> 14:08.806
If they're told to die,

14:08.890 --> 14:10.933
they'd gut themselves.
Look at their eyes.

14:12.352 --> 14:14.520
Are these guys insane?

14:14.604 --> 14:16.272
Look.

14:17.482 --> 14:18.775
In times like these,

14:18.816 --> 14:21.402
you need it to stay true
to your convictions.

14:21.486 --> 14:22.487
A little bit of madness.

14:22.570 --> 14:23.488
[sniffs]

14:25.281 --> 14:26.783
Now

14:26.824 --> 14:28.284
let's see...

14:29.744 --> 14:32.121
this so-called resolve of yours!

15:00.024 --> 15:01.275
[chuckles softly]

15:01.359 --> 15:04.487
[♪♪♪]

15:17.125 --> 15:18.376
[Hijikata]
Well...

15:22.088 --> 15:24.340
you are something else.

15:31.347 --> 15:32.974
[exhales]

15:37.019 --> 15:38.563
Interesting.

15:49.824 --> 15:51.909
[sword rings]

15:51.993 --> 15:53.995
A duel to the death.

15:58.415 --> 16:00.042
I accept.

16:00.084 --> 16:05.214
[♪♪♪]

16:05.256 --> 16:09.135
[Sagawa]
Hijikata, there's something
I'd like to ask you.

16:10.595 --> 16:13.097
What does the way of the samurai
mean to you?

16:14.724 --> 16:17.393
What a pointless question
to ask...

16:17.435 --> 16:18.561
[grunts]

16:21.230 --> 16:23.566
To bloom brilliantly,
then gracefully fall.

16:25.109 --> 16:27.361
That's what it means
to be a samurai, no?

16:30.198 --> 16:32.283
I knew I was fond of you.

16:33.367 --> 16:34.785
But...

16:34.869 --> 16:36.287
that's precisely why...

16:37.622 --> 16:40.333
I'll fight with everything
I have as a samurai!

16:56.474 --> 16:57.725
Bring it on.

17:01.354 --> 17:02.730
[drum booms]

17:20.873 --> 17:21.790
[grunts]

17:21.874 --> 17:23.584
[groans]

17:29.423 --> 17:30.633
[chuckles]

17:30.675 --> 17:33.886
As expected of the greatest
samurai in all of Japan.

17:33.970 --> 17:36.889
Is Toshi going to be okay?

17:36.973 --> 17:38.474
Your path as a samurai...

17:38.558 --> 17:41.602
I hope this is not
the best you can muster.

17:41.686 --> 17:43.396
Now my blood is boiling!

17:45.565 --> 17:48.067
This is where
the real fight begins.

17:51.696 --> 17:53.823
[exhales slowly]

17:53.906 --> 17:55.575
Oh?

17:55.658 --> 17:56.867
Hiraseigan.

17:56.951 --> 17:59.787
So he's ready
to stake everything

17:59.870 --> 18:01.247
on a mere duel, not bad.

18:01.330 --> 18:03.207
It'll be over quickly.

18:05.251 --> 18:06.502
How can you tell?

18:06.544 --> 18:10.131
Yamanami.
You can't even figure that out?

18:10.172 --> 18:12.508
From the start, defense
isn't even in their minds.

18:12.550 --> 18:16.012
When the force
of ten against ten collide

18:16.053 --> 18:18.222
and they'll shatter.

18:18.306 --> 18:21.142
[Todo] Then the outcome
of this match is...

18:22.351 --> 18:24.520
[Yamanami]
A mutual kill.

18:24.562 --> 18:27.315
[Nagakura]
They are both going to die?

18:29.317 --> 18:32.153
[breathing deeply]

18:38.034 --> 18:39.744
Hey, Sagawa...

18:40.453 --> 18:41.412
Huh?

18:43.914 --> 18:45.833
Let us bloom with all our might.

18:47.168 --> 18:48.628
[yells fiercely]

18:52.089 --> 18:55.885
[♪♪♪]

18:55.968 --> 18:57.345
Hold it!

18:58.763 --> 18:59.847
The match is over.

19:02.433 --> 19:05.353
What are you talking about?
This fight isn't over yet!

19:05.436 --> 19:07.021
My Lord!
Let us fight till the end--

19:07.104 --> 19:08.439
[gunshot]

19:11.275 --> 19:12.610
You bastard...

19:15.154 --> 19:16.906
Are you screwing with me!

19:16.989 --> 19:19.075
Hey, you bastard!

19:19.158 --> 19:21.452
What,
you suddenly decided dying here

19:21.535 --> 19:23.788
wouldn't do Aizawa any good?
Huh?

19:25.039 --> 19:26.791
Don't you dare
go on the defensive!

19:30.127 --> 19:31.253
[gun cocks]

19:32.254 --> 19:33.923
That's how you die.

19:42.556 --> 19:44.350
[gun clicks]
[gasping sigh]

19:47.645 --> 19:49.897
I have no excuse.

19:55.653 --> 19:56.696
Hijikata.

20:02.368 --> 20:04.245
Your desperate,
all-or-nothing style...

20:04.328 --> 20:05.496
It was magnificent.

20:08.165 --> 20:09.458
Heh.

20:12.002 --> 20:13.838
I welcome you

20:13.921 --> 20:18.509
as the fools who are ready
to die alongside the Aizu!

20:26.684 --> 20:28.477
You all got that?

20:29.645 --> 20:32.857
From now on,
we live and die with them.

20:32.940 --> 20:34.483
We share one fate.

20:37.027 --> 20:38.946
There will be no objections.

20:39.029 --> 20:40.156
[all] Sir!

20:40.197 --> 20:43.993
[♪♪♪]

20:44.076 --> 20:45.745
[narrator]
And so, we were officially

20:45.828 --> 20:48.706
taken under the wing
of the Aizu clan

20:48.789 --> 20:52.209
and the Mibu Roshigumi

20:52.293 --> 20:56.005
later to become
the Shinsengumi, was born.

20:56.088 --> 20:57.381
[clamoring happily]

20:57.465 --> 20:59.675
[Sasaki] Kamo.
[Serizawa] Huh?

20:59.717 --> 21:01.427
I just
remembered.

21:01.510 --> 21:02.470
What?

21:02.553 --> 21:04.513
I can't stand
that guy.

21:05.723 --> 21:08.809
He was the same way
when he fought me.

21:08.893 --> 21:11.353
Utterly reckless.

21:11.437 --> 21:13.939
He has absolutely
no fear of death.

21:15.524 --> 21:18.527
Maybe that just means you don't
have enough resolve, Tada.

21:18.611 --> 21:20.488
[laughs]

21:21.655 --> 21:22.656
Rise!

21:25.743 --> 21:26.786
Bow.

21:34.585 --> 21:39.924
[Kusaka]
The time has finally come,
has it not, Takechi?

21:42.927 --> 21:46.597
Now that Shogun Iemochi
has traveled to the capital

21:46.680 --> 21:49.934
the shogunate has no choice
but to promise the Emperor

21:50.017 --> 21:51.602
they'll expel the foreigners.

21:53.270 --> 21:55.606
But the Aizu are a problem.

21:56.774 --> 21:59.443
I hear a group
called the Mibu Roshigumi

21:59.527 --> 22:01.779
is hunting the Aizu Hunters.

22:02.696 --> 22:03.823
CHOSHU RETAINER KUSAKA GENZUI

22:03.906 --> 22:05.199
The most dangerous one

22:05.241 --> 22:08.327
is Serizawa Kamo
a rogue from the Mito domain.

22:08.410 --> 22:12.164
And Kondo Isami
from the Shieikan, too.

22:12.248 --> 22:13.666
TOSA RETAINER TAKECHI HANPEITA

22:14.625 --> 22:16.919
And there's one more...

22:18.546 --> 22:22.800
The man who's rumored to have
defeated Sagawa Kanbei of Aizu.

22:22.883 --> 22:26.887
Just a rumor, of course.

22:26.971 --> 22:30.015
No matter who it is,
if they dare stand in our way...

22:32.309 --> 22:36.063
You understand
what must be done, Kusaka.

22:36.146 --> 22:38.482
Rest assured.

22:40.734 --> 22:42.444
I know

22:42.486 --> 22:47.741
their every move.

22:48.409 --> 22:51.537
[♪♪♪]

22:58.669 --> 23:00.504
[Aizu retainer 1]
Someone's coming.

23:00.588 --> 23:02.798
[Aizu retainer 2]
It could be that killer.

23:09.013 --> 23:09.930
[groans]

23:11.557 --> 23:14.602
So, you boys are from Aizu, huh?

23:14.643 --> 23:17.313
This pathetic?
You're hardly a challenge.

23:17.396 --> 23:20.149
You bastard!
Is it us Aizu you're after?

23:20.232 --> 23:21.901
I'm a Aizu Hunter.

23:21.984 --> 23:24.987
The Aizu Hunter?
I'm here to hunt down

23:25.070 --> 23:27.114
every last one
of you rotten shogunate dogs.

23:27.197 --> 23:28.157
SATSUMA RETAINER TANAKA SHINBEI

23:28.198 --> 23:29.658
You'd better be ready to die.

23:29.700 --> 23:31.827
Blink, and you're a dead man.

23:31.911 --> 23:33.120
[yells fiercely]

23:36.165 --> 23:38.542
[crunching]

23:40.085 --> 23:41.170
Enjoy.

23:45.633 --> 23:48.510
[Hijikata] "The Aizu Hunter,"
my ass. Damn it!

23:49.637 --> 23:51.722
That's six men last night alone.

23:53.557 --> 23:55.517
Who the hell is doing this?

23:55.601 --> 23:59.188
[Nagakura] Hey, Toshi.
Take it easy.

23:59.271 --> 24:02.441
Our men were killed!

24:02.524 --> 24:04.568
How the hell
am I supposed to be calm?

24:06.695 --> 24:09.865
The expulsionists have to be
the ones pulling the strings.

24:12.076 --> 24:13.702
Those sons of bitches.

24:13.786 --> 24:15.454
Judging by the sword work,

24:15.537 --> 24:17.790
it's all the work
of a single man.

24:20.876 --> 24:23.879
[laughing]
Hey.

24:23.963 --> 24:25.464
What do you want?

24:25.547 --> 24:27.883
You seem to be
enjoying yourself, huh?

24:30.260 --> 24:33.806
Nah, I'd say
there are two of them.

24:33.889 --> 24:35.516
On what grounds?

24:35.599 --> 24:38.686
How can you not even get that?
Huh?

24:38.769 --> 24:40.688
The Aizu men in Kiyamachi
were all hit

24:40.729 --> 24:43.607
with a single killing blow
from the front.

24:43.691 --> 24:46.819
But the ones in Uradera
were ambushed from behind.

24:46.902 --> 24:50.572
Alright, alright.
Now we're talkin'.

24:50.614 --> 24:52.408
You've got good eyes.

24:52.449 --> 24:55.119
Look, it doesn't matter
who the killer is.

24:57.079 --> 24:59.957
They're the ones
who picked this fight.

25:00.040 --> 25:01.792
They are mocking us!

25:03.627 --> 25:05.004
So enough with the chatter.

25:05.087 --> 25:08.090
We just need
to go cut them all down. Right?

25:09.591 --> 25:11.093
Do whatever you want.

25:12.469 --> 25:15.597
[Serizawa chuckling]

25:15.681 --> 25:17.266
What's so damn funny?

25:19.560 --> 25:23.147
[Sagawa]
There are two Aizu Hunters,
and both are master swordsmen.

25:23.230 --> 25:24.773
They could show up at any time.

25:24.815 --> 25:26.692
Don't let your guard down
for a second.

25:26.775 --> 25:29.153
[Hijikata] Wipe that grim look
off your face.

25:29.236 --> 25:30.612
I'm tellin' you, I'll take down

25:30.654 --> 25:32.656
one or two of these
"Aizu Hunters" myself.

25:32.740 --> 25:34.908
[Sagawa] Talking big,
aren't we, Hijikata?

25:34.992 --> 25:37.244
[Kondo]
That's what's great about him.

25:37.286 --> 25:39.705
[Yamanami] I'd say he's more
likely to get seriously hurt.

25:39.788 --> 25:42.958
[Hijikata] Don't you worry.
I'm a man who always delivers.

25:43.042 --> 25:44.960
[Yamanami] Who said
they were counting on you?

25:45.044 --> 25:48.047
[Wada]
I believe in you, Hijikata!

25:48.130 --> 25:49.631
[Hijikata]
Whoa, where did that come from?

25:49.673 --> 25:52.134
[Sagawa]
Ever since he saw you beat me,

25:52.217 --> 25:54.678
he's been your biggest admirer.

25:56.096 --> 25:57.264
Oh.

25:57.347 --> 26:01.518
Why don't you ask him
about that thing, Hironojo?

26:01.602 --> 26:03.145
I'll see you later.

26:12.946 --> 26:13.989
Hey.

26:14.865 --> 26:16.366
What did you want to ask me?

26:16.450 --> 26:18.619
I...
I couldn't possibly ask.

26:18.702 --> 26:20.496
Don't be shy!

26:20.579 --> 26:22.164
Need me to take care of someone
for you?

26:22.206 --> 26:23.749
Oh, no.

26:23.832 --> 26:27.002
It's just my son was born
the other day

26:27.086 --> 26:29.797
and I was hoping
you would name him.

26:33.759 --> 26:35.719
You want me to name him?

26:35.803 --> 26:39.098
I want my son to grow up
to be strong, just like you.

26:41.642 --> 26:43.102
[sword draws]
[man] Hiyah!

26:43.185 --> 26:44.228
Boss!

26:45.813 --> 26:47.606
[yells fiercely]
Wait!

26:50.275 --> 26:51.902
[Kondo]
The Aizu Hunters, huh?

26:54.279 --> 26:56.406
[singing indistinctly]

26:56.490 --> 26:58.742
[sighs]

27:13.757 --> 27:15.217
I carry out...

27:16.885 --> 27:19.054
Heavenly Retribution.

27:19.096 --> 27:20.973
Took you long enough.

27:22.641 --> 27:24.059
All right. Bring it on.

27:24.101 --> 27:27.396
So you're Kondo Isami.

27:27.437 --> 27:29.273
To think you dodged
my surprise attack.

27:29.356 --> 27:30.774
You're just as good as they say.

27:30.858 --> 27:32.651
Were you after our boss?

27:32.734 --> 27:34.653
[Wada groaning]

27:36.029 --> 27:37.531
[Kondo]
He's still breathing!

27:37.614 --> 27:40.868
Boss! Go and help him!
This one's mine.

27:40.951 --> 27:43.036
I'm telling you,
he's a master swordsman.

27:43.120 --> 27:44.204
Yeah...

27:45.372 --> 27:46.456
I won't forgive him.

27:46.540 --> 27:47.666
[Kondo]
Let's go!

27:47.749 --> 27:51.044
There's no point
in running away now.

27:51.128 --> 27:53.422
I'll cut you down
and then chase them.

27:53.463 --> 27:54.423
Bring it on!

28:05.475 --> 28:06.852
[sighs, chuckles]

28:06.935 --> 28:10.063
It's been a while since
someone's managed to wound me.

28:11.648 --> 28:13.984
But somehow,
I don't like you.

28:17.863 --> 28:19.114
What's with that look?

28:19.198 --> 28:21.366
Those eyes say you've thrown
everything away.

28:21.450 --> 28:22.993
That's some boring violence.

28:25.996 --> 28:27.080
Oh well.

28:27.122 --> 28:29.791
Before you die,
give me your name, Aizu Hunter.

28:32.211 --> 28:33.879
Okada Izo.

28:35.088 --> 28:38.133
At least now, those eyes
have some life in them.

28:42.054 --> 28:43.597
Hey, Hirayama.

28:43.680 --> 28:45.849
What are you, a moron?

28:45.933 --> 28:48.769
Stay out of my fight,
Interfere and I'll kill you.

28:50.187 --> 28:51.355
My apologies.

29:03.700 --> 29:06.370
You're slow.

29:06.453 --> 29:09.122
[laughs]

29:09.206 --> 29:10.374
You too.

29:10.457 --> 29:15.587
[♪♪♪]

29:15.671 --> 29:19.007
Maybe are you the one?

29:19.091 --> 29:22.010
The one they say
defeated Sagawa Kanbei?

29:23.220 --> 29:24.137
Your name?

29:27.474 --> 29:28.934
Hijikata Toshizo.

29:45.701 --> 29:47.286
[Yamanami]
That way!

29:48.620 --> 29:52.916
I'll remember you,
Hijikata Toshizo.

29:53.875 --> 29:56.086
I'll kill you myself.

29:57.754 --> 30:00.007
[Yamanami] Hijikata!
[Sagawa] Are you okay?

30:02.301 --> 30:03.385
Hey!

30:08.640 --> 30:11.226
[footsteps approaching]

30:11.310 --> 30:12.853
[Kondo]
It's me.

30:16.606 --> 30:19.401
Boss, how is he?

30:19.443 --> 30:20.902
He's safe.

30:21.611 --> 30:22.863
He said he can't die

30:22.946 --> 30:25.449
until you've named his son
for him, Toshi.

30:25.532 --> 30:27.326
[chuckles]

30:27.409 --> 30:28.452
Good.

30:30.287 --> 30:31.496
[Niimi] So?

30:32.581 --> 30:34.249
The ones who attacked you...

30:34.333 --> 30:36.585
you sure they were
the Aizu Hunters, too?

30:37.753 --> 30:39.129
Yes.

30:40.088 --> 30:41.340
A two-sword style ambush.

30:41.423 --> 30:43.467
From his accent,
he was from Satsuma.

30:45.052 --> 30:49.139
My guy was from Tosa.
Name's Okada Izo.

30:50.807 --> 30:52.267
Okada Izo?

30:53.060 --> 30:55.020
What? You know him?

30:55.103 --> 30:57.439
An old sparring partner
from Edo.

30:57.481 --> 30:58.565
I see.

30:59.608 --> 31:00.776
It has to be a mistake.

31:00.859 --> 31:01.943
What kind of nonsense is that?

31:01.985 --> 31:03.236
HIRAYAMA GORO

31:03.320 --> 31:04.738
He just tried to kill
Master Serizawa!

31:04.821 --> 31:07.115
And your leader's life, too.

31:10.660 --> 31:13.372
The fact
that both of our commanders

31:13.455 --> 31:15.665
were attacked
at the very same time...

31:15.749 --> 31:17.167
NIIMI NISHIKI

31:17.250 --> 31:20.379
No matter how you slice it,
something's not right.

31:20.462 --> 31:22.589
What are you getting at?

31:22.672 --> 31:26.051
Someone on the inside leaked
our movements to the enemy.

31:26.134 --> 31:28.303
You're saying
a traitor is among us?

31:28.387 --> 31:29.513
I am.

31:30.847 --> 31:32.349
For an old friend

31:33.433 --> 31:35.602
for example.

31:39.189 --> 31:40.649
Are you picking a fight?

31:40.732 --> 31:42.317
Toshi would never do that!

31:42.401 --> 31:46.113
[Kondo] Niimi, that theory
doesn't hold up.

31:46.196 --> 31:47.489
If Toshi were a traitor,

31:47.572 --> 31:49.199
it wouldn't make sense
for him to be wounded.

31:49.282 --> 31:51.368
What if he got wounded
just to deceive us?

31:51.451 --> 31:54.454
Why the hell would I do
something so stupid?

31:58.708 --> 32:00.544
Can we really trust you?

32:00.627 --> 32:03.839
[♪♪♪]

32:03.880 --> 32:06.633
What gives?
Not you too, Yamanami.

32:06.716 --> 32:08.385
In Tosa

32:08.468 --> 32:11.012
I've heard of
the Tosa Loyalist Party.

32:11.054 --> 32:14.099
They're radical
imperial loyalists.

32:15.183 --> 32:18.728
Okada Izo may very well
be one of them.

32:21.314 --> 32:23.567
Are you serious?

32:23.650 --> 32:25.777
[sighs]

32:25.861 --> 32:28.447
So, what's it gonna be?

32:30.198 --> 32:32.075
What're you gonna do
if that killer

32:32.159 --> 32:34.411
turns out to be your friend,
Okada Izo?

32:36.121 --> 32:39.583
When he comes to kill you,
what are you going to do then?

32:39.666 --> 32:41.126
Hmm?

32:49.843 --> 32:52.762
You hesitate, you die.

32:52.846 --> 32:54.097
Right?

32:57.767 --> 33:02.272
That's going too far,
Serizawa.

33:05.859 --> 33:08.987
Now that's the look
I wanted to see.

33:09.070 --> 33:10.947
Hey, Kondo, you want a match?

33:11.031 --> 33:12.991
I don't mind doing it right now.

33:13.074 --> 33:14.201
I don't fight my own men.

33:14.284 --> 33:17.454
Is that right?
Still cold as ever.

33:19.289 --> 33:23.001
Whatever.
Alright, let's go for a drink.

33:28.715 --> 33:30.133
[door closes]

33:32.093 --> 33:34.471
[bird cawing]

33:37.265 --> 33:39.309
[Tanaka]
A damn shame.

33:41.269 --> 33:43.396
Letting that man get away...

33:45.815 --> 33:47.484
[Seki]
You mean Kondo Isami?

33:47.567 --> 33:49.277
No.

33:49.361 --> 33:51.696
The man I crossed swords with.

33:53.323 --> 33:56.535
The one who's rumored
to have defeated Sagawa Kanbei.

33:58.495 --> 34:00.330
His name was...

34:01.831 --> 34:03.583
Hijikata...

34:03.667 --> 34:04.751
Right.

34:05.835 --> 34:08.338
Hijikata Toshizo.

34:10.924 --> 34:12.342
Toshizo?

34:14.844 --> 34:18.514
You met Toshizo?

34:21.685 --> 34:23.562
So you know the guy.

34:25.188 --> 34:28.190
That man
is a real piece of work.

34:28.275 --> 34:30.235
The more you cross swords
with him,

34:30.318 --> 34:32.445
the stronger he gets.

34:32.529 --> 34:38.451
If he fights like that I want to
see just how strong he can get.

34:41.871 --> 34:44.123
That man is my prey.

34:45.375 --> 34:48.420
Next time,
I'll be the one to finish him.

34:59.556 --> 35:00.682
If you do

35:01.933 --> 35:03.727
I'll kill you.

35:05.061 --> 35:06.688
What's that supposed to mean?

35:07.897 --> 35:09.524
Because I made a promise.

35:10.358 --> 35:14.362
That we'd fight one more time.

35:16.323 --> 35:20.493
So you've crossed swords
with Hijikata, then.

35:22.954 --> 35:24.581
We fought

35:28.126 --> 35:29.586
and we became friends.

35:31.588 --> 35:32.756
Friends?

35:34.924 --> 35:37.260
[laughs]

35:37.344 --> 35:40.555
This is war, you fool!

35:40.639 --> 35:43.642
It's kill or be killed!
Becoming friends...

35:43.725 --> 35:46.853
That isn't war.
It's nothing but child's play!

35:46.936 --> 35:48.897
He's the enemy!

35:48.938 --> 35:50.607
You're wrong.

35:52.692 --> 35:55.862
Toshizo is the exception!

35:55.945 --> 35:58.865
We cut down our enemies.

35:58.948 --> 36:00.909
That is our way.

36:00.950 --> 36:02.786
We are manslayers.

36:14.130 --> 36:17.467
[Sagawa]
So he's the traitor...

36:20.470 --> 36:21.471
Sasaki.

36:22.764 --> 36:24.599
Is that really true?

36:26.101 --> 36:28.144
[Sasaki] Yes.

36:28.228 --> 36:30.772
He was the one
who tracked him down.

36:30.855 --> 36:32.399
There's no doubt about it.

36:36.152 --> 36:38.988
[Sagawa]
My Lord, what are your orders?

37:03.680 --> 37:06.141
[man laughing]

37:06.224 --> 37:07.892
You're way too jumpy.

37:10.186 --> 37:11.563
Toshi!

37:12.856 --> 37:13.857
Hajime...

37:14.858 --> 37:16.234
Hajime!

37:36.337 --> 37:38.965
[Harada] It's not like you
to lose your composure.

37:54.355 --> 37:59.277
It hurts to suspect
one of our own.

38:07.952 --> 38:11.706
Yamanami! Sanosuke! Hurry!

38:11.748 --> 38:12.957
Get over here, quick!

38:13.041 --> 38:14.292
Hajime?

38:14.375 --> 38:16.795
Yeah, it really is you.

38:16.878 --> 38:19.672
Whoa!
Hey, Eisaburo!

38:19.714 --> 38:20.924
[happy clamoring]

38:21.007 --> 38:23.009
How've you been?

38:23.092 --> 38:24.803
Hajime!

38:24.886 --> 38:27.096
[laughing]
[groans]

38:28.556 --> 38:30.809
You! Do you have any idea
how worried we were?

38:30.892 --> 38:33.394
No, really.
Where the hell have you been?

38:33.478 --> 38:36.397
After leaving Edo... getting by.

38:39.108 --> 38:41.694
Actually, more recently,
I heard the Mibu Roshigumi

38:41.778 --> 38:44.113
were making a name
for themselves.

38:44.197 --> 38:47.075
And that you guys
were among them.

38:47.116 --> 38:48.952
Knew you missed us.

38:50.119 --> 38:51.287
That's not it!

38:51.371 --> 38:54.541
Then what brings you
all the way out here?

38:54.624 --> 38:59.003
I happened to see
some tense-looking idiot I knew

38:59.087 --> 39:00.421
heading this way.

39:00.463 --> 39:02.423
Don't use me as an excuse,
you jerk.

39:02.507 --> 39:04.467
[exclaiming happily]

39:04.551 --> 39:06.761
Whoa! Hajime!
When did you get here?

39:06.845 --> 39:08.596
Hey, enough already.

39:08.680 --> 39:09.514
Gotcha!

39:09.597 --> 39:11.516
Go, Heisuke!
Hey, go for it!

39:11.599 --> 39:13.309
Crap.

39:13.393 --> 39:15.895
Hey, Heisuke, hang in there!

39:15.937 --> 39:17.355
Go on!
Hang on! Hang on!

39:17.438 --> 39:19.065
[Nagakura]
Take him down!

39:19.148 --> 39:22.110
[groaning]
[laughter]

39:22.193 --> 39:23.403
[Hijikata]
Give it back! Give it back!

39:23.486 --> 39:24.612
[Nagakura]
Show him!

39:40.795 --> 39:42.005
Enter.

39:57.103 --> 39:58.396
Hajime.

40:00.315 --> 40:02.525
You...
what is the meaning of this?

40:02.609 --> 40:06.404
Saito Hajime is a criminal
who has taken a man's life.

40:06.487 --> 40:08.281
We can't just let him run loose.

40:08.364 --> 40:11.701
On my authority,
until things cool down

40:11.784 --> 40:13.870
I've decided to place him
in the Aizu domain's custody.

40:15.413 --> 40:18.416
Sorry I didn't say anything.
Boss.

40:21.544 --> 40:22.837
Now, to business.

40:25.715 --> 40:27.926
It's about
the Aizu Hunters.

40:28.009 --> 40:29.719
As you know

40:29.802 --> 40:33.014
our moves are being leaked
to the enemy.

40:33.097 --> 40:34.265
Yes.

40:34.349 --> 40:36.935
I've identified the traitor.

40:38.061 --> 40:39.354
Eh?

40:39.437 --> 40:41.731
The one who uncovered him was...

41:00.917 --> 41:01.918
Boss.

41:08.758 --> 41:09.759
Hey, Boss.

41:11.928 --> 41:13.596
What's wrong?

41:18.851 --> 41:21.938
Are you all right?
You look pale.

41:23.147 --> 41:24.649
Hei, Shinpachi! Heisuke!

41:34.951 --> 41:36.160
[sniffs]

41:38.705 --> 41:40.540
The traitor has been identified.

41:43.960 --> 41:45.044
[sighs]

41:46.587 --> 41:47.964
Who is it?

41:50.466 --> 41:52.468
Spit it out.

41:52.552 --> 41:55.096
I'll beat them to a pulp myself.

41:55.179 --> 41:59.851
[♪♪♪]

42:12.864 --> 42:14.073
Hey, Eisaburo.

42:17.452 --> 42:18.786
Hajime.

42:24.333 --> 42:25.710
I'm so surprised.

42:25.793 --> 42:28.212
I can't believe
you were in Kyo this whole time.

42:32.800 --> 42:34.802
Hey, have you tried
the mitarashi dango

42:34.886 --> 42:36.637
from the Shimogamo Shrine yet?

42:36.721 --> 42:39.307
We'd sneak out of training
to eat them

42:39.390 --> 42:42.685
all the time back in Edo,
remember?

42:42.769 --> 42:46.314
We could only ever afford one,
so we'd always have to split it.

42:46.355 --> 42:48.191
They taste just like I remember.

42:52.820 --> 42:54.822
You haven't changed a bit.

42:57.283 --> 42:58.826
What's that supposed to mean?

43:01.079 --> 43:02.789
Why did you betray us?

43:04.040 --> 43:05.583
Huh?

43:05.666 --> 43:07.251
What are you talking about?

43:07.335 --> 43:09.378
It's no use playing dumb,
Eisaburo.

43:11.047 --> 43:15.093
I was under orders from Aizu
to investigate the Choshu clan.

43:18.054 --> 43:20.056
Why did you betray us?

43:21.432 --> 43:23.184
Huh?

43:23.267 --> 43:29.732
You were the one who always said
everyone at Shieikan is family.

43:44.288 --> 43:45.998
[scoffs]

43:46.082 --> 43:47.667
I had no choice.

43:48.876 --> 43:50.795
They said they'd tell me
where he was

43:50.878 --> 43:52.964
if I fed them our information.

43:54.006 --> 43:55.174
Where he was?

43:57.593 --> 44:00.930
The man who murdered my brother.

44:03.766 --> 44:05.852
Keep at it, Eisaburo.

44:05.935 --> 44:08.187
You have a real gift.

44:08.271 --> 44:10.064
You really think so?

44:10.106 --> 44:11.732
Yes.

44:11.816 --> 44:15.194
Mine! Come on, catch me!
Brother! Hey!

44:15.278 --> 44:16.362
[groans]

44:16.445 --> 44:17.697
Brother!

44:20.449 --> 44:21.951
[crying]

44:36.966 --> 44:39.969
I heard a rumor
that he was in Kyo...

44:42.638 --> 44:44.515
It was around that time

44:44.599 --> 44:46.976
we were all to go to Kyo.

44:48.895 --> 44:53.107
I searched for him in my free
time. All over the place.

44:53.191 --> 44:56.861
I heard he was spotted
in Shimabara pleasure district

44:56.944 --> 44:59.197
and checked them all.

45:02.867 --> 45:05.995
That's when I met him.

45:08.581 --> 45:10.124
A man from Choshu...

45:12.043 --> 45:13.461
Kusaka Genzui.

45:19.425 --> 45:21.219
You've been looking

45:21.302 --> 45:24.055
for someone in the pleasure
district, haven't you?

45:28.935 --> 45:31.979
I happened to see you
the other day.

45:32.063 --> 45:37.193
As a matter of fact, I may know
the person you're looking for.

45:43.866 --> 45:48.829
The man with the Asura tattoo,
correct?

45:48.913 --> 45:53.042
[♪♪♪]

45:56.170 --> 45:59.715
[Hajime] So, just to find
your brother's killer

45:59.799 --> 46:02.301
you sold out your own comrades?

46:05.888 --> 46:07.473
Why would you go that far?

46:15.648 --> 46:18.067
If it lets me
avenge my brother...

46:20.653 --> 46:22.238
I'll do whatever it takes.

46:30.037 --> 46:32.081
You're going to strike me down?

46:34.041 --> 46:35.501
This should be fun.

46:37.503 --> 46:39.213
Go on, try it.

46:52.351 --> 46:53.269
[grunts]

46:54.645 --> 46:57.815
I kept my promise.
Isn't it enough now?

46:57.898 --> 47:00.526
Where is the man
who killed my brother?

47:07.033 --> 47:09.869
Tomorrow, at dusk...

47:12.747 --> 47:17.585
The man you want
will be at Gokuraku-ji Temple.

47:33.851 --> 47:36.312
Is that really
all your conviction amounts to?

47:37.563 --> 47:39.940
If you're so desperate to go

47:39.982 --> 47:42.276
you'll have to go
over my dead body.

48:08.803 --> 48:10.221
[exhales sharply]

48:19.397 --> 48:20.981
Not even

48:21.899 --> 48:23.317
a single day.

48:23.818 --> 48:25.486
Huh?

48:25.528 --> 48:27.571
Every night...

48:27.655 --> 48:29.990
every single night...

48:30.032 --> 48:31.534
Night after night.

48:31.617 --> 48:35.371
I dream about it.
About what happened that day.

48:35.454 --> 48:38.916
Running away,
I felt so pathetic.

48:38.999 --> 48:40.793
So damn pathetic.

48:40.876 --> 48:43.254
I kept thinking
I should turn back,

48:43.337 --> 48:45.548
cross blades, and die.
Over and over.

48:45.631 --> 48:46.966
But my legs...

48:47.049 --> 48:49.552
my legs just wouldn't
listen to me.

48:51.095 --> 48:54.140
Then I started hearing
voices behind me.

48:54.223 --> 48:57.226
"Coward. Why did you run?

48:57.309 --> 49:00.312
Aren't you ashamed
you're the only one who lived?

49:01.897 --> 49:04.233
You should've died.

49:05.651 --> 49:07.570
You should die!"

49:10.781 --> 49:14.034
So please Hajime, let me go.

49:14.076 --> 49:17.788
[♪♪♪]

49:17.872 --> 49:21.584
Honestly,
I don't want to let you die.

49:26.881 --> 49:28.007
But...

49:29.758 --> 49:34.472
better you die by my hand
than by anyone else's.

49:38.601 --> 49:41.187
[groaning]

49:45.608 --> 49:47.318
[coughing]

49:47.401 --> 49:48.569
Eisaburo!

50:04.001 --> 50:07.129
[birds cawing]

50:15.513 --> 50:17.056
My brother...

50:18.474 --> 50:20.434
Abiru Seiichiro

50:20.518 --> 50:23.020
was a retainer
of the Tsushima-Fuchu domain

50:25.314 --> 50:27.441
a master of the Hokushin
Itto-ryu school.

50:29.985 --> 50:32.488
Was it you
who murdered my brother?

50:36.992 --> 50:38.410
I was.

50:56.512 --> 50:58.514
I'm going to avenge

51:01.517 --> 51:03.060
my brother.

51:07.439 --> 51:08.482
The Asura...

51:08.566 --> 51:09.817
Ah...

51:13.612 --> 51:20.369
So that coward brat
has grown a spine, has he?

51:21.537 --> 51:23.205
Niimi...

51:23.289 --> 51:26.500
I knew from the very beginning,
Abiru.

51:26.584 --> 51:31.505
That you were the same
cowardly brat from Mibu.

51:32.506 --> 51:33.674
Were you

51:33.716 --> 51:36.677
working for Kusaka
and Choshu this whole time?

51:36.719 --> 51:38.554
You've got it backwards.

51:38.637 --> 51:41.265
I was the one using him.

51:41.348 --> 51:46.729
All so Serizawa could seize
control of the Mibu Roshigumi.

51:46.812 --> 51:49.565
Everything
was for Serizawa?

51:49.648 --> 51:52.735
[stifled laughter]

51:52.818 --> 51:54.236
Oh, please!

51:54.320 --> 51:58.324
That violent meathead
is just a figurehead.

51:58.365 --> 52:03.495
He's nothing without me
pulling the strings.

52:03.537 --> 52:04.913
What do you mean?

52:04.997 --> 52:07.416
You still don't get it,
you stupid hick!

52:08.626 --> 52:11.045
Fools dance
in the palm of my hand,

52:11.086 --> 52:13.380
and history moves at my command.

52:13.464 --> 52:14.715
[cackles]

52:14.757 --> 52:18.052
I can't get enough of this!

52:18.093 --> 52:20.804
You and your brother,
and those idiots at Shieikan

52:20.888 --> 52:23.432
exist just to be used by me.

52:27.936 --> 52:29.480
Eh...?

52:30.147 --> 52:32.483
Hiraseigan stance?

52:34.109 --> 52:36.236
You think you can take me down

52:36.278 --> 52:39.490
with you with a pathetic stance
like that?

52:39.573 --> 52:41.116
Niimi.

52:41.200 --> 52:43.619
[♪♪♪]

52:43.702 --> 52:46.080
You bastard!

52:46.163 --> 52:50.167
Let's be careful now.

52:50.250 --> 52:56.423
You'll ruin the priceless sword
I stole.

52:58.592 --> 53:01.178
No... it can't be my brother...

53:04.181 --> 53:07.601
Secret Sword: Poison Scorpion.

53:07.643 --> 53:09.186
[groaning]

53:11.271 --> 53:13.524
It's coated with aconite poison.

53:13.607 --> 53:17.611
Works like a charm on hot-headed

53:17.653 --> 53:20.447
idiots like you!

53:20.489 --> 53:22.783
[shouting]

53:22.866 --> 53:25.285
And you call yourself a samurai?

53:25.869 --> 53:27.371
Huh?

53:29.039 --> 53:32.751
Samurai? Please.

53:32.835 --> 53:35.754
These days, the ones weak up
here are called samurai.

53:39.675 --> 53:42.094
So long... You fool.

53:42.177 --> 53:46.765
[Niimi moaning]

53:46.849 --> 53:51.812
So good!

53:51.854 --> 53:53.689
[gasping]

53:53.772 --> 53:55.149
[men exclaiming]

53:55.232 --> 53:56.650
[music playing]

54:09.580 --> 54:10.998
Dusk, huh?

54:13.709 --> 54:17.838
You are in a good mood.
Did something good happen?

54:17.880 --> 54:19.006
I wonder.

54:20.048 --> 54:22.301
Alright! I'm going to sing too!

54:22.384 --> 54:24.011
[all exclaim]

54:24.094 --> 54:27.389
[singing along]

54:34.438 --> 54:35.856
[Nagakura]
Eisaburo!

54:39.359 --> 54:40.903
Eisaburo!

54:42.112 --> 54:43.697
[Kondo]
Toshi!

54:43.781 --> 54:45.866
Any luck over there?

54:45.908 --> 54:48.118
No, how about you guys?

54:48.202 --> 54:49.578
He's nowhere to be found.

54:50.579 --> 54:52.331
Nothing over here, either.

54:52.414 --> 54:55.626
Where the hell did Eisaburo go?

54:59.421 --> 55:02.716
[Todo, panting] Hey!
Something terrible's happened!

55:04.676 --> 55:06.637
This was in
Eisaburo's belongings...

55:09.306 --> 55:10.516
A NOTE

55:23.111 --> 55:24.363
Eisaburo...

55:25.531 --> 55:27.908
Hey, Eisaburo! Hey! Hey!

55:27.991 --> 55:29.910
[Abiru]
To my fellow members
of the Shieikan.

55:29.993 --> 55:31.453
[Hajime]
Crap.

55:31.537 --> 55:32.871
Nine years ago...
Eisaburo.

55:32.955 --> 55:36.041
...my brother
was murdered by thugs.

55:36.124 --> 55:37.751
Let's go back.

55:37.793 --> 55:42.339
Not a day has gone by that
I haven't thought about it.

55:42.422 --> 55:44.800
I have lived
for nothing else...

55:44.883 --> 55:48.762
Let's go. Eisaburo, wake up.
...but to avenge my brother.

55:48.804 --> 55:50.472
Hey, wait! Don't die!
In my long search

55:50.556 --> 55:51.890
for his killer in Kyo
I met Kusaka Genzui...

55:51.974 --> 55:56.937
Hey! Don't die!
...of the Choshu clan.

55:57.020 --> 55:58.522
And so

55:58.605 --> 56:02.359
I betrayed the Aizu...

56:03.569 --> 56:05.612
"...and all of you,

56:05.696 --> 56:08.156
by leaking your movements
to Kusaka.

56:09.867 --> 56:11.994
All so he'd reveal
my brother's killer.

56:15.122 --> 56:17.416
I know my betrayal
is unforgivable.

56:19.126 --> 56:20.627
But it was something...

56:20.711 --> 56:23.630
I had to do, no matter the cost.

56:25.007 --> 56:27.801
Whether I succeed
in my vengeance or not

56:30.637 --> 56:32.848
by now,
I am no longer of this world.

56:32.931 --> 56:35.517
[♪♪♪]

56:41.815 --> 56:42.858
Kondo.

56:44.818 --> 56:45.861
Yamanami.

56:47.613 --> 56:48.572
Gen.

56:49.781 --> 56:51.742
Sanosuke.

56:51.825 --> 56:52.826
Nagakura.

56:53.869 --> 56:54.953
Heisuke.

56:57.205 --> 56:58.165
Soji.

56:59.791 --> 57:01.043
Hijikata.

57:02.377 --> 57:03.503
Hajime.

57:07.466 --> 57:09.718
The Shieikan was my home...

57:12.429 --> 57:13.972
and my family.

57:18.727 --> 57:19.853
Thank you

57:21.104 --> 57:22.606
for everything."

57:35.410 --> 57:36.578
Look.

57:37.663 --> 57:39.247
[Hajime]
Eisaburo...

57:39.331 --> 57:40.791
Hajime...

57:44.086 --> 57:45.462
Hajime!

57:47.839 --> 57:49.049
Eisaburo!

57:54.221 --> 57:55.764
The Choshu?

57:57.224 --> 57:59.309
So the Choshu clan
killed Eisaburo!

57:59.393 --> 58:00.894
Let it go, Toshi. Not now.

58:00.978 --> 58:01.979
The hell I will!

58:02.062 --> 58:03.021
Toshi...

58:04.606 --> 58:06.149
I'm begging you.

58:07.484 --> 58:09.403
For now,

58:09.486 --> 58:11.947
can't we just let him
rest in peace?

58:16.535 --> 58:18.036
Eisaburo...

58:19.788 --> 58:22.124
he's finally managed
to beat himself.

58:27.129 --> 58:31.675
Listen...
Did any of you know? This guy...

58:33.552 --> 58:35.053
Abiru Eisaburo...

58:37.347 --> 58:40.017
Abiru... Eisaburo...

58:41.768 --> 58:45.188
was one hell of a fighter.

58:45.272 --> 58:46.773
[chuckling]

59:11.339 --> 59:12.591
Well done.

59:13.842 --> 59:16.470
[narrator]
On April 6, 1863,

59:16.511 --> 59:18.764
Abiru Eisaburo fell.

59:19.598 --> 59:21.308
He was 21 years old.

59:22.768 --> 59:24.144
His murder was covered up.

59:24.186 --> 59:26.229
His death
officially ruled an illness.

59:26.313 --> 59:28.148
Good for you, Eisaburo.

59:28.190 --> 59:32.944
He would be known as the first
member of the Mibu Roshigumi

59:33.028 --> 59:37.199
and the first to fall in Kyo.

59:42.037 --> 59:43.955
[birds chirping]

01:00:03.058 --> 01:00:04.559
Sorry, Eisaburo.

01:00:04.643 --> 01:00:07.145
I'm borrowing this for a while.

01:00:16.905 --> 01:00:18.907
What's with that getup?

01:00:19.699 --> 01:00:20.992
[chuckles]

01:00:25.539 --> 01:00:26.957
These are for you guys.

01:00:36.883 --> 01:00:38.635
Light blue-green, huh?

01:00:40.595 --> 01:00:42.347
Apparently,
Serizawa had them made.

01:00:45.934 --> 01:00:47.727
It's the color
of the 47 Ronin's coats

01:00:47.811 --> 01:00:49.271
when they committed seppuku.

01:00:55.694 --> 01:00:58.155
He's telling us to be ready
to die at any moment.

01:01:12.669 --> 01:01:14.296
His death
will not go unanswered.

01:01:17.632 --> 01:01:19.092
I will see to that.

01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:28.435
Hajime.

01:01:30.770 --> 01:01:33.273
I'm not letting anyone else die
on my watch again.

01:01:39.529 --> 01:01:41.781
When we fall, we fall together.

01:01:41.823 --> 01:01:44.993
[♪♪♪]

01:02:07.974 --> 01:02:10.977
[narrator]
Because of Eisaburo's betrayal

01:02:11.019 --> 01:02:13.146
our boss was knocked out
of the running

01:02:13.188 --> 01:02:15.398
for leadership
of the Mibu Roshigumi.

01:02:17.192 --> 01:02:21.863
And so, Serizawa Kamo
was made Chief Commander.

01:02:23.740 --> 01:02:25.325
Hey, Niimi.

01:02:26.868 --> 01:02:30.372
Looks like you like
drawing things out.

01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:32.916
[chuckles]

01:02:32.999 --> 01:02:35.835
Well, dancing on them
isn't so bad either.

01:02:38.588 --> 01:02:39.923
Right?

01:02:46.179 --> 01:02:48.181
Was this really the right thing?

01:02:50.475 --> 01:02:52.352
I couldn't save Eisaburo.

01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:57.899
I'm not cut out to be a leader.

01:02:59.651 --> 01:03:00.902
But...

01:03:02.195 --> 01:03:05.198
I will get revenge for Eisaburo,
no matter what.

01:03:05.282 --> 01:03:08.827
[♪♪♪]

01:03:15.417 --> 01:03:20.046
[Kusaka]
Even now, it is seared
into the back of my mind.

01:03:21.756 --> 01:03:25.427
That hateful
American merchant ship,

01:03:25.510 --> 01:03:28.513
squatting in the Kanmon Strait.

01:03:29.931 --> 01:03:34.394
And our Choshu cannons
firing upon it!

01:03:34.436 --> 01:03:39.274
Boom! Boom! Boom! Kaboom!

01:03:39.357 --> 01:03:40.900
[cackling]

01:03:40.984 --> 01:03:45.822
It was a truly
exhilarating sight!

01:03:46.948 --> 01:03:48.867
Our preparations
against the Aizu

01:03:48.950 --> 01:03:50.577
are proceeding splendidly.

01:03:50.618 --> 01:03:54.205
However, it is not yet enough.

01:03:56.458 --> 01:03:58.585
[Takechi]
Do you have a plan in mind?

01:04:06.384 --> 01:04:10.764
The assassination
of Lord Anegakoji Kintomo.

01:04:10.847 --> 01:04:13.308
You want to kill one
of the Emperor's own aides?

01:04:13.391 --> 01:04:15.810
Lord Anegakoji was once
a passionate advocate

01:04:15.894 --> 01:04:17.437
for expelling the foreigners

01:04:17.479 --> 01:04:22.442
has now switched his allegiance
to the pro-opening faction.

01:04:22.484 --> 01:04:24.527
If we let this stand...

01:04:25.987 --> 01:04:29.366
But if we're the ones
to carry out

01:04:29.449 --> 01:04:31.701
his "divine retribution,"

01:04:31.785 --> 01:04:34.329
we'd make the Imperial Court
our enemy.

01:04:34.412 --> 01:04:35.663
Precisely.

01:04:37.665 --> 01:04:41.211
I have a plan for that.

01:04:43.463 --> 01:04:46.383
[♪♪♪]

01:05:08.571 --> 01:05:14.244
JUNE 17, 1863

01:05:19.207 --> 01:05:23.670
Lord Anegakoji Kintomo,
face divine retribution!

01:05:24.921 --> 01:05:27.048
[fierce yelling]

01:05:35.974 --> 01:05:37.851
[whimpering wheezily]

01:05:37.934 --> 01:05:39.269
[cries out]

01:05:42.397 --> 01:05:45.358
[♪♪♪]

01:06:03.251 --> 01:06:06.129
Hear ye, hear ye!
At Sarugatsuji Crossroads

01:06:06.212 --> 01:06:08.173
in the Flower Capital, Kyoto,

01:06:08.256 --> 01:06:10.842
Anegakoji Kintomo
has been cut down!

01:06:10.925 --> 01:06:13.052
The culprit? Shocking!

01:06:13.094 --> 01:06:15.430
A ruthless, bloodthirsty villain
slays shogunate

01:06:15.513 --> 01:06:18.766
retainers night after night!
Want to know who it is?

01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:20.310
Come and buy your copy!

01:06:20.393 --> 01:06:21.519
I want to know!

01:06:21.603 --> 01:06:24.189
[crowd clamoring]

01:06:24.272 --> 01:06:26.733
[Wada] Tanaka Shinbei!
Get him! Get him! Hold it!

01:06:32.780 --> 01:06:34.073
Where did he go?

01:06:43.041 --> 01:06:46.336
Tanaka Shinbei!
This time, I will kill you!

01:06:46.419 --> 01:06:47.962
You fellas...

01:06:48.046 --> 01:06:51.216
How'd you figure out
it was me?

01:06:51.299 --> 01:06:54.135
Because you left
your sword behind.

01:06:54.761 --> 01:06:56.137
My sword?

01:06:58.223 --> 01:07:00.141
You didn't notice?

01:07:03.978 --> 01:07:06.314
So that's it, huh?

01:07:08.024 --> 01:07:09.609
[yells fiercely]

01:07:19.869 --> 01:07:21.955
Even if you kill me...

01:07:22.038 --> 01:07:24.791
Hijikata will hunt you down
without fail.

01:07:26.501 --> 01:07:28.086
Hijikata?

01:07:29.295 --> 01:07:31.631
You mean Hijikata Toshizo!

01:07:31.673 --> 01:07:33.091
[laughs]

01:07:45.019 --> 01:07:46.813
Ah!

01:07:46.854 --> 01:07:48.022
Damn...

01:07:48.106 --> 01:07:49.440
Failed again.

01:07:50.316 --> 01:07:53.069
You've gotten better, Hijikata.

01:07:54.445 --> 01:07:55.947
Hey, Soji.

01:07:56.030 --> 01:07:58.157
Don't give me that crap.

01:08:00.702 --> 01:08:04.414
You got distracted and lost your
footing, didn't you?

01:08:09.002 --> 01:08:11.504
No, really. You have
gotten better, Hijikata.

01:08:12.714 --> 01:08:15.341
You never would have
noticed that before.

01:08:17.093 --> 01:08:19.595
If you've got something
on your mind, spit it out.

01:08:27.353 --> 01:08:29.229
It's about Serizawa Kamo.

01:08:31.524 --> 01:08:32.734
Right.

01:08:34.359 --> 01:08:36.904
He's been taking
the new recruits out,

01:08:36.988 --> 01:08:39.323
and they drink
nearly every night.

01:08:39.407 --> 01:08:40.116
Welcome.

01:08:40.198 --> 01:08:41.658
Welcome.
Hey.

01:08:41.743 --> 01:08:43.620
Welcome. This way, please.
[Okita] With that guy,

01:08:43.703 --> 01:08:44.912
our commander-in-chief

01:08:44.996 --> 01:08:47.206
while Kondo
gets treated like dirt...

01:08:53.046 --> 01:08:55.298
I just can't stand for it.

01:08:56.006 --> 01:08:58.134
[thunder rumbling]

01:08:58.216 --> 01:09:02.180
Soji,
I appreciate the sentiment.

01:09:02.220 --> 01:09:05.767
But what's important
isn't who's in charge.

01:09:07.268 --> 01:09:10.438
It's protecting Kyo
from the extremist imperialists.

01:09:19.947 --> 01:09:22.408
[running footsteps]
Hm.

01:09:23.076 --> 01:09:24.868
[gasping]

01:09:28.956 --> 01:09:32.251
Tanaka Shinbei's
killed another one!

01:09:36.631 --> 01:09:37.756
This way!

01:09:43.930 --> 01:09:45.264
[Okada] Brutal.

01:09:47.475 --> 01:09:48.643
[Aizu retainer]
Hironojo!

01:09:50.603 --> 01:09:52.104
Hironojo!

01:09:52.145 --> 01:09:54.440
Hironojo!
Are you all right?

01:09:54.524 --> 01:09:56.442
Yes. I...

01:09:56.526 --> 01:09:58.820
It's all right.
I'm glad you're alive.

01:09:58.903 --> 01:10:00.279
No, that's not it.
Don't speak!

01:10:00.321 --> 01:10:02.156
No, you don't understand!

01:10:02.240 --> 01:10:05.076
He let me live.

01:10:05.159 --> 01:10:06.619
Hijikata...

01:10:06.661 --> 01:10:09.122
so I could deliver
a message to you.

01:10:09.205 --> 01:10:10.790
What do you mean?

01:10:12.041 --> 01:10:14.627
Tanaka Shinbei is waiting.

01:10:14.669 --> 01:10:15.670
He's...

01:10:16.629 --> 01:10:18.548
waiting for you

01:10:18.631 --> 01:10:19.966
Hijikata.

01:10:21.676 --> 01:10:22.760
Where?

01:10:24.095 --> 01:10:26.347
Sanbonmatsu.

01:10:26.431 --> 01:10:27.849
Hold it, Hijikata.

01:10:27.932 --> 01:10:29.809
We're going with you.
[Yamanami] We're coming too.

01:10:29.892 --> 01:10:31.352
No. I'm going alone.

01:10:31.436 --> 01:10:32.979
You can't take him on alone.

01:10:33.020 --> 01:10:34.939
If we go together,
he'll just run.

01:10:36.482 --> 01:10:39.819
Besides, I won't stoop
to such cowardly tactics.

01:10:42.071 --> 01:10:43.990
I'll go with him.

01:10:44.031 --> 01:10:46.784
Boss!
Sagawa.

01:10:46.868 --> 01:10:48.494
Please let me go.

01:10:48.536 --> 01:10:51.539
If anything happens to Hijikata

01:10:51.622 --> 01:10:53.875
I swear I'll take him down.

01:10:57.003 --> 01:10:59.922
[♪♪♪]

01:11:09.557 --> 01:11:12.185
[Hijikata]
Boss, stay out of this.

01:11:12.268 --> 01:11:13.561
[Kondo] I know.

01:11:26.699 --> 01:11:27.992
Tanaka Shinbei!

01:11:29.494 --> 01:11:32.205
So you only brought
Kondo Isami with you?

01:11:32.288 --> 01:11:35.082
I figured you'd bring more men.

01:11:35.166 --> 01:11:38.336
Hijikata,
I have to admire your guts.

01:11:40.838 --> 01:11:43.925
So they threw you away,
just as I thought.

01:11:44.008 --> 01:11:45.301
What do you mean?

01:11:45.384 --> 01:11:48.054
Something about it
never sat right with me.

01:11:48.137 --> 01:11:51.641
Why would a master swordsman
like you leave his blade behind?

01:11:53.351 --> 01:11:55.603
But seeing your two-sword style,
now I'm sure of it.

01:11:55.686 --> 01:11:59.023
The sword you "forgot"
at Sarugatsuji was a fake.

01:12:00.441 --> 01:12:01.859
The imperialists
framed you

01:12:01.943 --> 01:12:05.029
to avoid being branded enemies
of the court.

01:12:06.823 --> 01:12:08.908
So what?

01:12:08.950 --> 01:12:11.118
I still did it.

01:12:11.202 --> 01:12:12.912
That doesn't change a thing.

01:12:14.622 --> 01:12:17.708
Draw your sword, Hijikata.

01:12:28.427 --> 01:12:30.096
Why the fixation on me?

01:12:31.389 --> 01:12:33.057
I decided that you,
and you alone,

01:12:33.140 --> 01:12:34.600
would be the one I cut down.

01:12:35.560 --> 01:12:38.104
Now, let's settle this.

01:12:45.820 --> 01:12:47.154
Bring it on.

01:13:06.299 --> 01:13:09.510
You kill people
just because you're told to

01:13:09.594 --> 01:13:12.305
then getting tossed aside
when you're no longer useful.

01:13:12.388 --> 01:13:14.849
That makes you nothing more
than a puppet!

01:13:16.017 --> 01:13:18.644
I don't understand a thing
about politics.

01:13:18.728 --> 01:13:19.937
But...

01:13:20.021 --> 01:13:23.482
I have killed
in the name of my own justice.

01:13:23.566 --> 01:13:25.860
Shogunate or Court,
if something's rotten,

01:13:25.943 --> 01:13:27.153
I'll set it right.

01:13:27.194 --> 01:13:29.113
That is the cause I fight for.

01:13:30.281 --> 01:13:32.074
What kind of justice is that?

01:13:33.492 --> 01:13:35.494
I don't care what you call it.

01:13:36.537 --> 01:13:38.873
You're still just a murderer!

01:13:41.000 --> 01:13:42.460
Isn't a fight

01:13:43.544 --> 01:13:45.713
supposed to be
honor against honor

01:13:46.881 --> 01:13:49.091
something more passionate
than this?

01:14:26.837 --> 01:14:27.964
[grunting]

01:14:28.047 --> 01:14:30.925
I was born poor,
the son of a boatman.

01:14:37.390 --> 01:14:42.269
All I ever wanted
was to be a samurai!

01:14:46.732 --> 01:14:49.026
To be called a killer...

01:14:50.319 --> 01:14:52.655
an honor not everyone can claim,
is it?

01:14:52.738 --> 01:14:55.908
So a boatman's son
can't become a samurai?

01:14:55.950 --> 01:14:57.201
Just watch me.

01:14:58.828 --> 01:15:01.622
I'll cut them down,
again and again and again.

01:15:02.832 --> 01:15:07.420
And if that changes
the course of history

01:15:07.503 --> 01:15:10.172
our names
will be remembered forever.

01:15:10.256 --> 01:15:13.050
As the true samurai
who set this rotten world right.

01:15:15.928 --> 01:15:17.138
I get it.

01:15:18.723 --> 01:15:20.599
But it's all so pointless.

01:15:43.539 --> 01:15:45.875
I'm the son of a farmer, too!

01:15:48.335 --> 01:15:50.755
We're not so different,
you and I.

01:15:50.838 --> 01:15:53.215
The thrill is in doing
what others can't.

01:15:53.299 --> 01:15:55.509
I feel the same way.

01:15:55.593 --> 01:15:57.636
But... making a name
for myself in history

01:15:57.678 --> 01:15:59.346
I couldn't care less
about any of that.

01:15:59.430 --> 01:16:01.891
I just want to fight
strong opponents.

01:16:01.974 --> 01:16:04.727
As long as I can fight
someone strong

01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:07.063
that's all that matters.

01:16:08.731 --> 01:16:09.982
It's the only time

01:16:11.108 --> 01:16:12.735
I feel truly alive.

01:16:14.403 --> 01:16:16.155
Like right now, fighting you.

01:16:19.533 --> 01:16:21.744
My blood is pounding
in my veins.

01:16:29.335 --> 01:16:31.337
We're a couple of fools,
aren't we?

01:16:33.047 --> 01:16:34.840
Both of us.

01:16:36.383 --> 01:16:38.886
[both chuckling]

01:16:50.606 --> 01:16:53.275
[♪♪♪]

01:16:54.401 --> 01:16:55.319
[yells fiercely]

01:17:09.458 --> 01:17:10.918
This is...

01:17:11.001 --> 01:17:12.336
my defeat.

01:17:15.422 --> 01:17:16.632
I see now...

01:17:17.550 --> 01:17:19.844
why Izo saw something in you.

01:17:21.137 --> 01:17:22.096
Izo...

01:17:23.347 --> 01:17:24.849
You know him?

01:17:28.185 --> 01:17:29.145
Yeah.

01:17:30.062 --> 01:17:33.983
He said you two were friends.

01:17:37.653 --> 01:17:41.323
I've never had a friend
in my life.

01:17:43.826 --> 01:17:48.747
That's why I wanted to kill you.

01:17:50.833 --> 01:17:54.211
Maybe I was even jealous of Izo.

01:17:59.633 --> 01:18:01.302
I'm glad

01:18:02.386 --> 01:18:04.847
my final opponent was you...

01:18:16.984 --> 01:18:18.194
Shinbei!

01:18:21.322 --> 01:18:24.283
[♪♪♪]

01:18:37.671 --> 01:18:40.174
That could have been me.

01:18:47.765 --> 01:18:50.142
If I hadn't met you all...

01:19:37.648 --> 01:19:39.066
Tanaka Shinbei.

01:19:43.320 --> 01:19:45.531
I have etched your name
upon my soul.

01:20:11.390 --> 01:20:13.183
[yawns]

01:20:15.269 --> 01:20:17.354
[Niimi] I can't believe
Hijikata was the one

01:20:17.396 --> 01:20:18.689
to take down Tanaka Shinbei.

01:20:18.772 --> 01:20:20.357
[Serizawa]
I like it.

01:20:20.441 --> 01:20:23.152
He just keeps getting
more interesting.

01:20:24.069 --> 01:20:25.821
This is going to be fun.

01:20:27.990 --> 01:20:31.243
[narrator] Satsuma clansman
Tanaka Shinbei's body

01:20:31.285 --> 01:20:34.330
was given
to the magistrate's office

01:20:34.413 --> 01:20:37.333
and his death
was officially ruled suicide

01:20:37.416 --> 01:20:38.751
during questioning.

01:20:38.834 --> 01:20:42.796
This was to appease
the Satsuma domain

01:20:42.880 --> 01:20:45.924
which had friendly ties
to the shogunate.

01:20:45.966 --> 01:20:51.263
[♪♪♪]

01:20:51.305 --> 01:20:53.974
998!

01:20:58.312 --> 01:21:00.356
999!

01:21:05.819 --> 01:21:07.154
1,000!

01:21:21.835 --> 01:21:24.254
[Kondo]
You're still at it, I see.

01:21:27.132 --> 01:21:29.259
It helps clear my head.

01:21:31.678 --> 01:21:33.263
Yeah, I know what you mean.

01:21:38.310 --> 01:21:39.603
Back in Edo

01:21:42.189 --> 01:21:44.566
I didn't need
to do practice swings

01:21:48.153 --> 01:21:51.031
to keep my mind clear.

01:21:58.622 --> 01:22:00.207
Will our family...

01:22:04.044 --> 01:22:06.547
end up disappearing
one by one someday?

01:22:09.716 --> 01:22:11.385
Like Eisaburo...

01:22:13.137 --> 01:22:15.222
I wonder
what Izo's up to.

01:22:18.851 --> 01:22:20.978
Once they decide
he's no longer useful...

01:22:23.188 --> 01:22:25.190
will they just
cast him aside?

01:22:27.860 --> 01:22:29.570
Like they did
with Tanaka Shinbei.

01:22:34.741 --> 01:22:36.493
Damn it.

01:22:41.415 --> 01:22:45.544
At first, all I wanted was
to be stronger than you, Kondo.

01:22:50.424 --> 01:22:51.550
Toshi...

01:22:52.759 --> 01:22:54.344
the times are changing.

01:22:57.014 --> 01:22:58.974
In this chaotic era,

01:23:01.018 --> 01:23:03.270
what can I really accomplish
with my sword?

01:23:05.731 --> 01:23:07.149
I want to find out,

01:23:07.232 --> 01:23:09.526
together with everyone
from the Shieikan.

01:23:14.239 --> 01:23:17.701
We've finally made a name
for ourselves...

01:23:17.784 --> 01:23:19.995
This is just the beginning,
Toshi.

01:23:22.915 --> 01:23:24.458
For our family,

01:23:26.668 --> 01:23:28.128
this is just the beginning.

01:23:44.436 --> 01:23:45.562
But

01:23:47.272 --> 01:23:49.525
if it's too much,
you can always walk away.

01:23:52.903 --> 01:23:54.613
Like hell I will.

01:23:57.157 --> 01:24:00.327
I'm not quitting
until I've beaten you.

01:24:10.546 --> 01:24:13.632
[♪♪♪]

01:24:13.674 --> 01:24:16.343
[shouts]

01:24:27.521 --> 01:24:28.480
[exclaims]

01:24:35.487 --> 01:24:38.323
[♪♪♪]

01:24:38.407 --> 01:24:39.658
[laughing]

01:24:41.910 --> 01:24:43.245
Damn!

01:24:44.037 --> 01:24:45.497
[sighs]

01:24:45.539 --> 01:24:47.165
Impressive.

01:24:48.208 --> 01:24:51.211
You always push me
to get stronger.

01:24:53.338 --> 01:24:55.591
But you won't be smiling
for long.

01:24:55.674 --> 01:24:57.342
[laughing]

01:24:57.384 --> 01:25:00.387
[laughing] Look who's talking!
You're smiling too.

01:25:00.470 --> 01:25:01.555
Alright!

01:25:04.558 --> 01:25:06.018
Hiya!

01:25:06.101 --> 01:25:07.436
[all] Hiya!

01:25:08.562 --> 01:25:09.730
[all] Hiya!

01:25:11.064 --> 01:25:12.524
[all] Hiya!

01:25:14.234 --> 01:25:15.611
[all] Hiya!

01:25:17.070 --> 01:25:18.739
[Kondo] One!
Hiya!

01:25:18.822 --> 01:25:20.657
Two!
Hiya!

01:25:21.825 --> 01:25:23.785
One!
Hiya

01:25:24.703 --> 01:25:26.538
Two!
Hiya!

01:25:28.498 --> 01:25:29.541
[all] Hiya!

01:25:29.625 --> 01:25:30.667
Two!

01:25:30.751 --> 01:25:31.668
[all] Hiya!

01:25:39.009 --> 01:25:40.594
[Seki]
Pardon the intrusion.

01:25:45.599 --> 01:25:49.519
[♪♪♪]

01:25:56.276 --> 01:25:59.738
[all chattering]

01:25:59.821 --> 01:26:02.449
Yeah! Awesome!

01:26:11.917 --> 01:26:14.211
[laughing]

01:26:14.294 --> 01:26:16.755
[Katamori's aide]
Kondo Isami.

01:26:16.838 --> 01:26:22.594
For your patriotic service
and sincere loyalty

01:26:22.636 --> 01:26:27.099
as a member
of the Mibu Roushigumi

01:26:27.182 --> 01:26:29.643
you are hereby appointed
its commander.

01:26:29.726 --> 01:26:31.937
We expect you
to continue to serve

01:26:32.020 --> 01:26:33.480
with the utmost diligence.

01:26:37.401 --> 01:26:38.985
[Doshin]
Hold it! Found him!

01:26:48.370 --> 01:26:50.372
Yah!
[all] Aah!

01:26:55.001 --> 01:26:57.421
[♪♪♪]

01:27:21.653 --> 01:27:24.573
[wind whistling]
[straw rustling]

01:27:30.746 --> 01:27:33.290
[shuddering gasps]

01:27:46.344 --> 01:27:48.722
[grunting]

01:27:57.063 --> 01:27:58.982
[panting]

01:28:02.235 --> 01:28:03.487
[panting]

01:28:03.570 --> 01:28:05.238
[Ichikawa, breathlessly]
Excuse me?

01:28:05.322 --> 01:28:08.742
Where exactly are we going?

01:28:08.825 --> 01:28:10.035
1912, HAKODATE

01:28:11.328 --> 01:28:14.122
How much longer
is this going to take?

01:28:14.206 --> 01:28:15.749
[Nagakura] What?

01:28:15.832 --> 01:28:18.084
For someone so young,
you're pathetic.

01:28:20.420 --> 01:28:22.589
What's with that old geezer?

01:28:24.216 --> 01:28:27.427
[Nagakura]
It's been a while, Toshi.

01:28:31.056 --> 01:28:32.307
[sighs]

01:28:33.558 --> 01:28:35.894
I've brought some guests today.

01:28:35.936 --> 01:28:38.313
She wants to hear
about the Shinsengumi...

01:28:38.396 --> 01:28:40.482
Your story, actually.

01:28:40.565 --> 01:28:44.611
She came because she wants to
hear Hijikata Toshizo's stories.

01:28:58.375 --> 01:29:00.168
It's a pleasure to meet you.

01:29:00.252 --> 01:29:02.170
I'm Makoto Ichikawa.

01:29:02.254 --> 01:29:05.173
Who gets nervous at a grave?

01:29:05.257 --> 01:29:06.508
Sorry.

01:29:12.305 --> 01:29:14.099
Honestly, I'm surprised.

01:29:15.559 --> 01:29:17.894
What Nagakura told us

01:29:17.936 --> 01:29:22.399
was so different from my idea
of the Shinsengumi.

01:29:22.482 --> 01:29:25.944
The story changes
depending on who's telling it.

01:29:27.153 --> 01:29:28.655
True.

01:29:30.490 --> 01:29:32.826
Why aren't you asking me
any questions?

01:29:34.661 --> 01:29:36.746
You don't know anything about me

01:29:36.830 --> 01:29:38.999
other than that
I came from Tokyo.

01:29:40.333 --> 01:29:42.168
So why did you decide
to tell me?

01:29:47.090 --> 01:29:48.466
You...

01:29:48.508 --> 01:29:50.677
Toshi's granddaughter,
aren't you?

01:29:51.845 --> 01:29:53.722
How?

01:29:53.805 --> 01:29:54.848
When?

01:29:56.850 --> 01:29:59.519
That snowy day
when we first met.

01:30:01.354 --> 01:30:03.189
You had the same eyes as Toshi.

01:30:06.943 --> 01:30:11.072
[♪♪♪]

01:30:11.156 --> 01:30:15.702
No one in my family would ever
tell me about my grandfather.

01:30:16.703 --> 01:30:18.163
Of course
they wouldn't.

01:30:19.623 --> 01:30:22.500
We, the Shinsengumi,
were called rebels...

01:30:22.584 --> 01:30:24.586
enemies
of the Imperial Court.

01:30:24.669 --> 01:30:26.922
Hijikata Toshizo
was the vice commander.

01:30:27.005 --> 01:30:28.840
If anyone knew
you were related to him,

01:30:28.924 --> 01:30:30.508
who knows
what you would've faced.

01:30:30.592 --> 01:30:33.470
Even so, I have to know
about my grandfather.

01:30:34.596 --> 01:30:38.058
His blood,
the blood of Hijikata Toshizo

01:30:38.141 --> 01:30:40.101
flows through my veins.

01:30:45.398 --> 01:30:46.900
So that makes you

01:30:48.610 --> 01:30:51.071
a "thorny brat",
just like him, huh?

01:30:52.113 --> 01:30:54.783
[chuckling softly]

01:30:58.244 --> 01:31:01.748
Now then, please go on.

01:31:06.544 --> 01:31:08.755
To bloom in battle

01:31:10.256 --> 01:31:12.008
and to fall in battle.

01:31:15.136 --> 01:31:18.390
Samurai are flowers
that bloom in full splendor,

01:31:18.473 --> 01:31:20.558
unafraid to fall.

01:31:22.560 --> 01:31:26.481
The Shinsengumi
were the last flowers to bloom

01:31:26.564 --> 01:31:30.902
in the dying twilight
of the Bakumatsu era.

01:31:30.944 --> 01:31:32.779
Charge!

01:31:34.614 --> 01:31:38.785
[Yoshiaki Dewa's "Chiruran
Shinsengumi Requiem" playing]
